              <h2 class="mb-4">How does a Decentralized Crypto Wallet Work?</h2>
              <p>A decentralized crypto wallet is simply a crypto wallet you manage and maintain
                yourself.
                Decentralized wallets aren't provided by a third party service provider. Instead, they exist on your
                computer or removable drive, cutting third-party services out of your transactions. Decentralized
                wallets allow pure peer-to-peer digital transactions over the internet.Simply put, the ability to
                transact peer-to-peer is important for security, privacy, and independence, as peer-to-peer
                transactions help eliminate the threat of corporate or government surveillance. Deployed over a
                blockchain network, the wallet infrastructure is hosted over millions of nodes with no single point of
                failure.</p>
            </div>
